    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, ITEM C, DOING BUSINESS AS:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>CALIFORNIA SCHOOLS BENEFITS TRUST</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 8B:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION DOES NOT HAVE ANY COMMITTEES WITH AUTHORITY TO ACT ON BEHALF OF THE GOVERNING BODY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ADMINISTRATOR PERFORMS THE INITIAL REVIEW OF THE FORM 990 AND VERIFIES THE INFORMATION TO THE AUDITED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS. THE FORM 990 WAS REVIEWED IN DETAIL WITH THE BOARD PRIOR TO FILING WITH THE IRS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ALL TRUSTEES MUST ANNUALLY SUBMIT SIGNED DISCLOSURES TO BOTH CO-CHAIRS OF THE ORGANIZATION INDICATING THAT THEY WILL ABIDE BY THE REQUIREMENTS SET FORTH IN THE CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY. IF THERE IS A KNOWN CONFLICT OF INTEREST, THE AFFECTED INDIVIDUAL IS DISQUALIFIED AND MUST RECUSE HIM/HERSELF FROM THE DECISION MAKING PROCESS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION MAKES ITS FINANCIAL STATEMENTS, GOVERNING DOCUMENTS AND CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY AVAILABLE TO THE PUBLIC UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VII, SECTION A, LINE 1A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TRUSTEES ARE NOT COMPENSATED BY THE TRUST. TRUSTEES ARE EMPLOYED BY THE CONTRIBUTING SCHOOL DISTRICTS OR SPONSORING ORGANIZATIONS (CALIFORNIA TEACHERS ASSOCIATION AND CALIFORNIA SCHOOL EMPLOYEES' ASSOCIATION) (RELATED ORGANIZATIONS). INFORMATION REGARDING COMPENSATION PAID TO TRUSTEES BY THE SCHOOL DISTRICTS CAN BE REQUESTED FREE OF CHARGE FROM THE SCHOOL DISTRICTS (REFER TO SCHEDULE R OF THE FORM 990 FOR A LIST OF THE CONTRIBUTING SCHOOL DISTRICTS) IN ACCORDANCE WITH CALIFORNIA GOVERNMENT CODE SECTION 6250 THROUGH 6276.48 OF THE CALIFORNIA PUBLIC RECORDS ACT. COMPENSATION PAID TO TRUSTEES BY THE SPONSORING ORGANIZATIONS (CALIFORNIA TEACHERS ASSOCIATION AND CALIFORNIA SCHOOL EMPLOYEES' ASSOCIATION) IS REPORTED ON THE FORM 990 FILED WITH THE INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE BY THE RELATED TAX-EXEMPT ORGANIZATION. IF YOU WOULD LIKE ADDITIONAL INFORMATION, PLEASE CONTACT THE THIRD-PARTY ADMINISTRATOR, RISK PROGRAM ADMINISTRATORS, A GALLAGHER COMPANY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART XII, LINE 2C:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD OF TRUSTEES HAS RESPONSIBILITY FOR OVERSIGHT OF THE AUDIT AND SELECTION OF AN INDEPENDENT ACCOUNTANT. THIS PROCESS HAS NOT CHANGED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
